Be less hasty, don't burn up all of your magic marker or wand of
wishing charges on stuff you don't need because then you won't have it
for something that you do need.  If I can swing it, I save two wishes
for the last minute, 1 for a cockatrice corpse at the beginning of
Astal and 1 for a helm of opposite alignment when I'm standing on the
wrong altar.

If you've got genocide scrolls to burn then you can take out R and use
an uncursed scroll to take out [insert correct spelling of master mind
flayer here, or is it master mindflayer, nono, it's mr. Mind Flayer,
no wait ...].  Or alternatively wait until you get to the plane of
water and blessed genocide ;.

Which named demons do you expect to have trouble with?  I would
recommend killing Orcus with a cockatrice corpse or after hitting with
a potion of paralysis while wearing a ring of free action so that you
get his wand with a minimum of charges expended.  The other 3 are
pushovers and require at most (for all 3): 10 gp, a wand of digging,
and a blessed unicorn horn.

Your AC is fine in general but a minotaur could still make pretty
short work of you so be careful.  I'd go ahead and use up your enchant
armor scrolls but wouldn't use magic marker charges to make anymore
until just before the run and you know you have extra charges for the
planes.  Go ahead and go into Gehennom, it's not very dangerous
because you can always run away.  I always feel a lot safer with
teleportitis and teleport control, though.

Have fun!  Good luck and good skill!
